## Tier-2 Publish Plane

Editor exposes scenes to T2/T3 through `derivePublishedSurface(graph) → PublishedPipeline | { errors }` — pure, framework-agnostic. See `publish-plane.mdc`.

- **`publishRoot`** (output, pass-through TEXTURE) marks the scene entry point. Exactly one allowed; zero/multiple → hard error. Params: `name` (display), `version` (author-bumped), `effectId` (slug — primary key consumers route on).
- **`tapZone`** (animTrigger, CONTOUR → EVENT) is a runtime tap source bounded by an upstream contour. Editor EMIT button stands in for the platform's hit-test. Stable `id` (autogen `tap_<n>`) — Tier-3 routes dispatches on it. `eventEmitter` extended with the same `id` / `label` so both event sources share the dispatch contract.
- **Per-node `data.exposed`** (`{ mode: 'whole' | 'fields', fields?, label?, hint? }`) decides what the supplier sees. `mode='whole'` renders the existing NodeView in the supplier app (Image, Segmentation); `mode='fields'` (currently only meaningful for `config`) lists individual `FieldDef` checkboxes. Lives on each node so it survives PublishRoot deletion + copy-paste.
- **Right-rail `PublishInspector`** picks up canvas selection from RF's store; surfaces the right widget per processor — toggle for whole-node nodes, per-FieldDef checkboxes for `config`, live publication summary when PublishRoot is selected.
- **`derivePublishedSurface`** — `resolveSceneForEngine(pages)` flattens clones, BFS reverse-walks edges from the root, classifies reached nodes into `imageSlots[] / tapZones[] / fields[] / wholeNodes[]`, validates (no orphans, unique tap ids, non-empty effect id), trims graph to reached subgraph. Output is the Tier-2/Tier-3 contract; bumping `PUBLISH_MANIFEST_VERSION` is breaking for both consumers.
- **Bottom Pin Terminal** replaces the right-rail pin sidebar — pinned nodes stack horizontally as IDE-style terminal cards along the editor's bottom edge. Toolbar gets dedicated Inspect / Pins toggles + Publish button.

