## Scene Persistence

### Dexie DB (`effects-scene-db`)

Two tables:
- `snapshots` (`++id, timestamp`): `SceneSnapshot { pages?, activePageId?, nodeIdCounter, manifestVersion?, timestamp, label, pinnedIds?, /* legacy: */ nodes?, edges?, viewport? }`. New writes always populate `pages` and `manifestVersion: PUBLISH_MANIFEST_VERSION`; legacy snapshots without `manifestVersion` default to `1` on read.
- `blobs` (`key, updatedAt`): `BlobEntry { key, blob, mime, width?, height? }`.

`SerializedPage = { id, name, nodes: SerializedNode[], edges: SerializedEdge[], viewport? }`. `SerializedNode.data` carries `cloneOf?: string` (UI-only viewer alias — never `engine.addNode`'d) and `exposed?` (Tier-2 supplier-exposure metadata). See `persistence.mdc`.

### SceneStore API

Snapshots: `pushSnapshot` (auto-trim to MAX_SNAPSHOTS=80), `undo`, `redo`, `currentSnapshot`. Cursor-based.
Blobs: `putBlob`, `putDataUrl`, `getBlob`, `getBlobUrl`, `getDataUrl`, `deleteBlob`.
Housekeeping: `clearAll`, `clearSnapshots`.

### History Flow

1. `useSceneHistory` debounces (1200 ms) after any pages / active-page / pin change.
2. Serialises multi-page state → `SerializedPage[]` plus global `nodeIdCounter` / `pinnedIds` / `activePageId`. Active page captures fresh viewport via `getViewport()`; inactive pages keep their last-saved viewport.
3. Persists image blobs (data URLs → IndexedDB) and segmentation masks. Walks every page; clones skipped.
4. Pushes snapshot. Undo/redo restore via `applySnapshot` → `replaceScene(pages, activePageId)` → re-hydrate engine for non-clone nodes only.

### Node ID Counter (defensive sync)

Node IDs follow `n_<int>`, minted by `nextId` in `node-editor/constants.ts`. Counter must never fall behind the live max suffix — otherwise `nextId()` hands out a duplicate, RF dedupes by `id`, original gets silently dropped.

Three guards: `applySnapshot` syncs to `Math.max(snap.nodeIdCounter, maxNodeIdNumber(snap.nodes))`, `addNode` runs the same heal just before minting, `exportScene` writes the live counter (not `0`).

