## UI Architecture

### NodeEditor.tsx

Orchestrates: `useSceneState` (multi-page state — `pages`, `activePageId`, page CRUD), `engineRef`, four custom hooks, toolbar, page-tab strip, sidebar, context menu. RF renders the active page only; engine sees the full scene through `resolveSceneForEngine(pages)`. Loading gate shows "Initializing GPU..." until Pixi is ready.

### Multi-page scenes & clones

Named pages (tab strip in `NodeEditorTabs`); each page owns its `nodes/edges/viewport`. Originals live on the page they were created on. Clones (`cloneOf` set) are UI-only viewer aliases of an original anywhere in the scene — no input handles, mirror the original's outputs, never reach the engine. Originals editable inline (double-click header); the new label propagates to clones via `useScene().findOrigin`.

Single engine sync: `useEffect(() => engine.setEdges(resolveSceneForEngine(pages).resolvedEdges), [pagesStructuralHash, engineReady])`. Hash includes only `(node id, processor type, cloneOf, edges)` and ignores viewport / page name / ordering — the gate prevents page-switch freezes. `addNode` / `removeNode` only for real nodes; cycle prevention at connect time via `wouldCreateCycle(pages, source, target)`.

Clone insertion lives in `SceneOutlineSidebar` (left rail) — drag a row onto the canvas. `AddNodePopover` carries only fresh-processor items.

### BaseNodeShell.tsx

Renders `NodeResizer` (selected, grid-snapped), coloured header (accent from category via CSS `--pn-accent`), input/output `<Handle>`s at 20px row pitch, widget area, pin toggle. Header title editable in graph mode (double-click); shows `REF` badge when `isClone`. Two modes: **graph** (full chrome + handles) and **headless** (no handles/resizer — pin terminal). In headless mode `HeadlessNodeDataProvider` reflects renames live.

### EditableStepEdge.tsx

Custom orthogonal edge with draggable bend points. Bend data persists in `edge.data.bends`.

### Node Views

One per processor + `CloneNodeView` (UI alias — viewer-only, derives outputs from the original). Each wraps `BaseNodeShell` and renders parameter widgets via `widgets/`. Engine via `useEngine()`; params via `useSetParam()`.

### Category Colours

8 live hues: green (input) → gold/orange/pink (animTrigger / animMod / animCtrl) → blue (imageOp) → teal (contour) → red (output) → slate (util). 6 legacy aliases (`depth` sky, `ai`/`marigold`/`dnf` violet, `source` green, `process` blue) keep persisted scenes from going grey but don't appear in the live menu. All accents sit on the dark side of the perceived-luminance line so unified light header text reads cleanly.

